{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1381 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "2830a8be2b560e0bdf918c2a58a82e1e65a4626610444198c733b56a40de0e3d" :edb/db-before-t 1380 :edb/db-after-t 1381 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534693 50 #inst "2026-10-08T04:21:47.212Z" 13194139534693 true] [17592186105634 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303714 13194139534693 true] [17592186105634 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303721 13194139534693 true] [17592186105635 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303728 13194139534693 true] [17592186105635 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303735 13194139534693 true] [17592186106112 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534693 true] [17592186106112 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nGiven the function $f(x) =-x^{4} + 2x^{3} + 6$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $x = 0$ is a local maximum\n2. $x = 0$ is neither a local minimum nor a local maximum\n3. $x = \\frac{3}{2}$ is a local maximum" 13194139534693 false] [17592186106112 1100 "Given the function $f(x)=-{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+6,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=0$ is a local maximum\n- $x=0$ is neither a local minimum nor a local maximum\n- $x=\\frac{3}{2}$ is a local maximum" 13194139534693 true] [17592186106112 1145 "First, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}=-4{x}^{2}(x-\\frac{3}{2}).\n$$\n\nSolving ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n-4{x}^{2}(x-\\frac{3}{2})=0\\,⟹\\,x=0\\,\\text{or}\\,x=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo we have two stationary points, $x=0,\\,\\frac{3}{2}.$ Next, to determine whether these points are local maxima or minima, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-1,1,2$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & =-4(-1)^{2}(-1-\\frac{3}{2})=10>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(1) & =-4(1)^{2}(1-\\frac{3}{2})=2>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =-4(2)^{2}(2-\\frac{3}{2})=-8<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,0)$ | $0$ | $(0,\\frac{3}{2})$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $(\\frac{3}{2},\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-1$ |  | $1$ |  | $2$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $0$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ |\n| $f$ | $↗$ |  | $↗$ | max | $↘$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical points.\n\n- At $x=0,$ the first derivative does not change the sign. Therefore, $x=0$ is neither a local minimum nor a local maximum.\n\n- At $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ the first derivative changes sign from positive to negative. Therefore, $x=\\frac{3}{2}$ is a local maximum.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303714 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303715 13194139534693 true] [17592186303714 1089 "q-113763" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303714 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534693 true] [17592186303714 1100 "Given the function $f(x)={x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+3x-2,$ which of the following statements are true?" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303714 1113 #uuid "c3b542e7-13bb-5855-a1b4-10e9a704f0b5" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303714 1145 "First, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =3{x}^{2}+6x+3 \\\\  & =3({x}^{2}+2x+1) \\\\  & =3(x+1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n3(x+1)^{2}=0\\,⇒\\,x=-1.\n$$\n\nSo $x=-1$ is the only stationary point of $f(x).$ Next, to determine whether this point is local maximum or minimum, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-2,0$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-2) & =3(-2+1)^{2}=3>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & =3(0+1)^{2}=3>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,-1)$ | $-1$ | $(-1,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-2$ |  | $0$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↗$ |  | $↗$ |\n\nThe first derivative does not change sign at $x=-1.$ Therefore, we conclude that $x=-1$ is neither a minimum nor a maximum.\n\nHence, the first derivative test shows that the function has no local extrema." 13194139534693 true] [17592186303715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303716 13194139534693 true] [17592186303715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303717 13194139534693 true] [17592186303715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303718 13194139534693 true] [17592186303715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303719 13194139534693 true] [17592186303715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303720 13194139534693 true] [17592186303715 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534693 true] [17592186303715 1041 "selection" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303715 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303718 13194139534693 true] [17592186303715 1110 #uuid "f79a16b8-7f2e-5f88-9ef5-c49a8f45e94d" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303716 1034 "There is a local minimum at $x=-1$" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303716 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534693 true] [17592186303716 1111 #uuid "e1552ced-b2c9-56e1-9d95-9d1a59cab06f" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303717 1034 "There is a local minimum at $x=1$" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303717 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534693 true] [17592186303717 1111 #uuid "542f6be2-8c2a-5816-959a-01278e6f8720" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303718 1034 "The function $f(x)$ has no local extrema" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303718 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534693 true] [17592186303718 1111 #uuid "a45f1826-9181-53e6-816e-ed1c1f38cb65" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303719 1034 "There is a local maximum at $x=-1$" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303719 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534693 true] [17592186303719 1111 #uuid "62e50f6b-6b56-5970-9cb5-c4dfdcb2678b" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303720 1034 "There is a local maximum at $x=1$" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303720 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534693 true] [17592186303720 1111 #uuid "e6fac620-ec34-5793-8587-67c80fe8f909" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303721 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303722 13194139534693 true] [17592186303721 1089 "q-113765" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303721 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534693 true] [17592186303721 1100 "Given the function $f(x)=7-{x}^{7},$ which of the following statements are true?" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303721 1113 #uuid "85c5d136-bff0-5d6f-b8b5-5a061746fd98" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303721 1145 "First, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-7{x}^{6}.\n$$\n\nSolving ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n-7{x}^{6}=0\\,⟹\\,x=0.\n$$\n\nSo $x=0$ is the only stationary point of $f(x).$ Next, to determine whether this point is local maximum or minimum, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-1,1$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & =-7(-1)^{6}=-7<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(1) & =-7(1)^{6}=-7<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,0)$ | $0$ | $(0,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-1$ |  | $1$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $-$ | $0$ | $-$ |\n| $f$ | $↘$ |  | $↘$ |\n\nThe first derivative does not change sign at $x=0.$ Therefore, we conclude that $x=0$ is neither a minimum nor a maximum.\n\nHence, the first derivative test shows that the function has no local extrema." 13194139534693 true] [17592186303722 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303723 13194139534693 true] [17592186303722 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303724 13194139534693 true] [17592186303722 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303725 13194139534693 true] [17592186303722 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303726 13194139534693 true] [17592186303722 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303727 13194139534693 true] [17592186303722 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534693 true] [17592186303722 1041 "selection" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303722 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303726 13194139534693 true] [17592186303722 1110 #uuid "0ad9f6ea-5b1a-500e-ab5e-07129d025c23" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303723 1034 "There is a local minimum at $x=0$" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303723 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534693 true] [17592186303723 1111 #uuid "439e25f7-5d47-57e7-bae8-6b921ff83669" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303724 1034 "There is a local minimum at $x=7$" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303724 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534693 true] [17592186303724 1111 #uuid "07522304-f2ac-58fe-ad99-ef8d85bbc088" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303725 1034 "There is a local maximum at $x=7$" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534693 true] [17592186303725 1111 #uuid "62e6e85b-ac53-521d-a8ee-e27f130d65a0" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303726 1034 "The function $f(x)$ has no local extrema" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303726 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534693 true] [17592186303726 1111 #uuid "baf6a1c6-6d62-5136-bf55-eb7242a42ef6" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303727 1034 "There is a local maximum at $x=0$" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303727 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534693 true] [17592186303727 1111 #uuid "4779cb38-451c-50cb-b14a-57526c3a2a1e" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303728 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303729 13194139534693 true] [17592186303728 1089 "q-22754" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303728 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534693 true] [17592186303728 1100 "For the function $f(x)=\\frac{x-1}{{x}^{2}-2x+2},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=0$ is a local minimum\n- $x=1$ is a local minimum\n- $x=2$ is a local maximum" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303728 1113 #uuid "31ae5e63-813a-51de-aa8d-389cb224f1d2" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303728 1145 "First, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{(1)\\cdot ({x}^{2}-2x+2)-(x-1)\\cdot (2x-2)}{({x}^{2}-2x+2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x+2-2{x}^{2}+4x-2}{({x}^{2}-2x+2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{x}^{2}+2x}{({x}^{2}-2x+2)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{x}^{2}+2x}{({x}^{2}-2x+2)^{2}} & =0 \\\\ -{x}^{2}+2x & =0 \\\\ x(2-x) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $x=0$ and $x=2$ are stationary points. Next, to determine whether these points are local maxima or minima, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-1,1,3$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & =\\frac{-(-1)^{2}+2(-1)}{((-1)^{2}-2(-1)+2)^{2}}=-\\frac{3}{25}<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{-(1)^{2}+2(1)}{((1)^{2}-2(1)+2)^{2}}=1>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & =\\frac{-(3)^{2}+2(3)}{((3)^{2}-2(3)+2)^{2}}=-\\frac{3}{25}<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in the table shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,0)$ | $0$ | $(0,2)$ | $2$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-1$ |  | $1$ |  | $3$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ |\n| $f$ | $↘$ | min | $↗$ | max | $↘$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical points.\n\n- At $x=0,$ the first derivative changes sign from negative to positive. Therefore, $x=0$ is a local minimum.\n\n- At $x=2,$ the first derivative changes sign from positive to negative. Therefore, $x=2$ is a local maximum.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303729 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303730 13194139534693 true] [17592186303729 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303731 13194139534693 true] [17592186303729 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303732 13194139534693 true] [17592186303729 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303733 13194139534693 true] [17592186303729 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303734 13194139534693 true] [17592186303729 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534693 true] [17592186303729 1041 "selection" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303729 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303731 13194139534693 true] [17592186303729 1110 #uuid "7dcbf80f-5823-5249-bb0f-d4b6d38fa677" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303730 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303730 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534693 true] [17592186303730 1111 #uuid "5b9de64c-9838-55a8-9ef6-fc47990c9621" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303731 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303731 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534693 true] [17592186303731 1111 #uuid "c59833bb-6c9a-5fa1-b388-9fe96c8732ed" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303732 1034 "I only" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303732 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534693 true] [17592186303732 1111 #uuid "5a54aba1-813a-58f8-b4e7-4e3d46c7fe4a" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303733 1034 "III only" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303733 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534693 true] [17592186303733 1111 #uuid "be3b8759-5f1c-5bcd-bf4b-26de86634f61" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303734 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303734 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534693 true] [17592186303734 1111 #uuid "69f1cf46-1e79-5193-8eb7-d5d0fb283371" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303735 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303736 13194139534693 true] [17592186303735 1089 "q-314706" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303735 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534693 true] [17592186303735 1100 "For which value of $x$ does the function $f(x)=(x-1)^{2}{e}^{x}$ have a local minimum? Do not round the answer.\n\nThe local minimum is at $x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534693 true] [17592186303735 1113 #uuid "f5607589-4cc2-5871-a40a-4c3842dcb8f7" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303735 1145 "First, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(x-1)^{2}\\cdot {e}^{x}+2(x-1){e}^{x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(x-1)(x-1+2) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(x-1)(x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving ${f}^{′}(x)=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}(x-1)(x+1) & =0 \\\\ (x-1)(x+1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-1,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $x=-1$ and $x=1$ are stationary points. Next, to determine whether these points are local maxima or minima, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-2,0,2$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-2) & ={e}^{-2}(-3)(-1)=3{e}^{-2}>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & ={e}^{0}(-1)(1)=-1<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & ={e}^{2}(1)(3)=3{e}^{2}>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,-1)$ | $-1$ | $(-1,1)$ | $1$ | $(1,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-2$ |  | $0$ |  | $2$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↗$ | max | $↘$ | min | $↗$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical points.\n\n- At $x=-1,$ the first derivative changes sign from positive to negative. Therefore, $x=-1$ is a local maximum.\n\n- At $x=1,$ the first derivative changes sign from negative to positive. Therefore, $x=1$ is a local minimum.\n\nWe conclude that $f(x)$ has a local minimum at $x=1.$" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303736 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303737 13194139534693 true] [17592186303736 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534693 true] [17592186303736 1041 "field-1" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303736 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303737 13194139534693 true] [17592186303736 1110 #uuid "5eecc1d2-90cc-551c-a730-ad4009139afd" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303737 1034 "1" 13194139534693 true] [17592186303737 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534693 true] [17592186303737 1111 #uuid "e6cde382-2326-5e06-b5fb-04ce4c30ead2" 13194139534693 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-113763" 17592186303714 "q-113763/selection" 17592186303715 "q-113763/selection/8868f02215a5337e2a5129e75503fbec783bb64f355b374ffdd731bd6e356bdb" 17592186303716 "q-113763/selection/acc83c74f03748b2e35d16f5b1d34df696d35c1cc9214487ece6a3d7d0147310" 17592186303717 "q-113763/selection/c112c665879534c7ad1d1042a8b28b7e5f3f70117c93b42716ffdd8ce86d808a" 17592186303718 "q-113763/selection/d9b70cb012b8a98348e0eb2b076c0ffaa03d2f9b5ed0b778c333cec60818df33" 17592186303719 "q-113763/selection/f6a9948068396877505e54f66bfd517f08252fd5fcfe067bfbdff6bc25b00dda" 17592186303720 "q-113765" 17592186303721 "q-113765/selection" 17592186303722 "q-113765/selection/3